    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras look primed for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by a pair of elite plays in **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Trea Turner** (79.40). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our top priority; facing Randy Dobnak, who carries a shaky 5.16 xERA, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill efficiency and favorable wind conditions that justify his status as an elite start. Similarly, **Trea Turner** projects to feast against Shane Bieber (5.23 xERA), with the optimizer leaning heavily into his elite speed and the high-leverage #2 spot in the order. Joining them in the top tier, **Kyle Schwarber** (78.21) remains a must-start, providing substantial power upside in that same matchup against Bieber, while **Yordan Alvarez** (65.05) remains an auto-lock despite the lack of a specific opposing pitcher data point, given his elite 0.471 xwOBA.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Lars Nootbaar** (46.60), who narrowly missed the starting cut to **Chase Meidroth** (46.54) and **Carson Benge** (47.50). While **Lars Nootbaar** offers a solid floor, the optimizer favored the specific dynamic platoon edges present for **Chase Meidroth** against Joey Cantillo. We continue to monitor the status of **Caleb Durbin**, who remains out of the lineup, and **Casey Schmitt**, who is unavailable due to an IL stint. Owners should exercise caution with **Dillon Dingler** (40.09); his score is hovering near our bench threshold, and while he is projected in the #3 hole, his efficiency is hampered by a significant negative platoon split against Logan Webb. With **Gary Sanchez**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Junior Caminero**, **Christian Yelich**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** rounding out the depth, we remain well-positioned for the 5x5 race, provided we carefully manage these marginal plate appearances to protect our game caps.",
